-- title:
--   Pole-chart place is pinned by the reduction relation
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \ge 1$ and a prime $\ell$, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose residue field $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$ has characteristic $\ell$, and let $\mathrm{fm}$ be a fibre model of level $N$ over $A$ with reduction map $\mathrm{residue}\,A : A \to k$: that is, subrings $B_{\mathrm{Fin}}, B_{\mathrm{Inf}}$ of the function field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\cdot F_N \subset \overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ containing the constants from $A$, with $j$ and $j_N$ in $B_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ and $j^{-1}$ in $B_{\mathrm{Inf}}$, both integral over the respective affine bases, together with ring maps $\pi_{\mathrm{Fin}}, \pi_{\mathrm{Inf}}$ onto the characteristic-$\ell$ field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ k\ N$ carrying constants to their residues and $j, j_N$ to $\bar j, \bar j_N$. Assume the cusp chart condition $\mathrm{cc}$: $j_N j^{-N} \in B_{\mathrm{Inf}}$ with $\pi_{\mathrm{Inf}}(j_N j^{-N}) = \bar j_N \bar j^{-N}$. Assume given, for each nonzero $d \mid N$, modular polynomial data for $d$ (a monic $\Phi_d \in \mathbb{Z}[x][y]$ of $y$-degree $\psi(d)$ with $\Phi_d(j, j_d) = 0$), and that the reduction of $\Phi_N$ to $k$, viewed over $k(x)$, is separable. Let $R$ be a regular prolongation of $A$ to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\cdot F_N$ with values in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ k\ N$ (a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ lying over $A$, with surjective residue map whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $\mathrm{residue}\,A$ on constants, and such that every nonzero element has a scalar multiple with nonzero residue), and assume $R$ is computed coefficientwise on $q$-expansions: every $y \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ with $A$-integral coefficients that lies in the function field belongs to $R.\mathrm{integers}$, and its $R$-residue is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $P$ be a place of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\cdot F_N$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ at which $j$ attains no $A$-integral value, in the sense that $\mathrm{ord}_P(j - a) \le 0$ for every $a \in A$, and let $Q$ be a place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ k\ N$ over $k$. Suppose finally that for every $h \in R.\mathrm{integers}$ integral over the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$ and every $a \in A$, the relation $h - a \in$ (non-units of the valuation subring of $P$) implies $R.\mathrm{residue}(h) - \overline{a} \in$ (non-units of the valuation subring of $Q$). Then the specialisation $\mathrm{fm.spPlace}$ of $P$, formed with the surjectivity of $A \to k$, the data $\Phi_d$ and the separability hypothesis, equals $Q$.
--
--   This is the uniqueness statement for reduction of places modulo a prime divisor of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in the chart where $j$ has a pole: the reduction relation, tested only on functions integral over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}[1/j]$, already determines the specialised place. Together with its companion at places centred at an $A$-integral value of $j$ it identifies the specialisation of an arbitrary place, and it is used in assembling the specialisation map on places and in comparing it with the place specialisation attached to a model.
